WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.392 --> 00:00:03.142
(dramatic music)

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:08.430
- [Woman] Growing up Mormon.

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:09.680
- [Man] Growing up in Yelyas Church.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:10.850
- [Woman] Being Mormon.

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:13.780
- [Man] I felt like being
gay just wasn't an option.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.330
- [Woman] We were about as
evil as a thing can get.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.370
- [Man] The church hasn't
really acknowledged us.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.740
- [Man] I was ultimately
told to suppress it.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.740
- [Woman] I dealt with
a lot of self-hatred.

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:26.713
- [Man] I thought about suicide a lot.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.830
- Utah's problem is that our

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:32.981
suicide rate has been climbing in youth,

00:00:32.981 --> 00:00:35.453
and that's appalling.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.850
- These kids are being lost,

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.590
but there's no discussion in the church.

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:44.050
As Mormons we need to have
some serious discussions, and

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:46.750
look in the mirror and figure
out what we're doing wrong.

00:00:47.927 --> 00:00:50.500
- The church has made it fairly clear

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:53.800
where they stand on gay relationships,

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.220
and so if you can't get on this ship,

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.220
those of us that are in the trenches

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.780
are gonna make it happen.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.583
And that's what Mama Dragons do.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:09.320
- It's very cool to see
this grass root network

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:13.263
of women giving people hope,
and giving people answers.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.310
- In the book, How To Be
a Perfect Mormon Mother,

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.123
there's no chapter, how
to parent your gay kid.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.373
Mama Dragons is helping
to right that chapter.

00:01:29.148 --> 00:01:31.731
(string music)

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.310
- Before my son came out,

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:38.513
I felt like being gay was an abomination.

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:42.393
I felt like it was a choice.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.573
I didn't really ever question anything.

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:50.560
I was asked by my leaders
to canvas my neighborhood

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:53.260
and get signatures to protect the marriage

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:55.020
between man and a woman.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:57.423
And I was a good little soldier.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:03.013
My whole thought process
changed when my son came out.

00:02:05.769 --> 00:02:08.440
- The Mormons tend to be a
pretty conservative bunch,

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:12.650
socially, and current
Mormon doctrine and policy,

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:15.840
really doesn't have a place

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.163
for the our LGBT kids.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.160
- A lot of people are fearful that

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:25.020
having their LGBT kids will impact

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.930
their relationship with the church,

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:30.110
it may impact their
standing with the church,

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:31.400
they're not willing to reach out

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.573
and go to the next step.

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:36.900
- For a lot of Mormon moms,

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:38.840
having a kid come out is the start

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:41.270
of a real faith crisis for them.

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:54.780
Mama Dragons is a support group

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:57.933
for Mormon moms with LGBT children.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:03.300
One of the things it does
is help moms not feel alone,

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:06.213
not feel like they're the
only one walking that path.

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:11.586
We figured out that
Grayson was transgender

00:03:11.586 --> 00:03:13.530
when he was 16 about halfway through

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:15.080
his junior year of high school.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:19.690
I was, you know, supportive
of his transition,

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:22.330
but for about the first year and a half,

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:25.950
I didn't know a single other, Mormon mom,

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.123
with a transgender kid.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:31.503
I don't want other moms to
feel as alone as I felt.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.640
- In five years, 10
years, if the Mama Dragons

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:39.653
still exist, we can have a huge base.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:44.070
There's usually 10-15,
every week that we add,

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:47.200
so that's 60 new women a month so,

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.293
720 a year.

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:55.480
- Most Mama Dragons that
I work with and know,

00:03:55.480 --> 00:04:00.480
have their finger and their
pulse on at least 15 kids.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.830
Talking through how they
might be able to come out

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:06.050
to their parent or how
to handle their situation

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.693
with their parents.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.240
Part of that is, you know, trying to

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:15.320
help them with suicide
prevention, understanding.

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:18.773
We're saying, oh no, that's
not gonna happen on my watch.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.260
- You know an average of 557

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:34.363
Utahans die by suicide every year.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:38.030
It is the leading cause of death

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:40.367
in youth ages 10-17 in Utah.

00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:42.730
(dramatic music)

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:43.910
- No one is acknowledging

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:47.700
that our LGBTQ people feel so ostracized,

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:49.750
by the religion that they were raised in.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:55.870
- Here, by default,

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:59.000
if you don't fit in your church community,

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.960
you then don't fit into your neighborhood

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:04.483
and then you don't fit into your school.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:09.200
- The data is very clear,

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.940
that young people who don't
have a good support network,

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:15.300
in particular young
people who feel rejected

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:18.653
by their families, are
at much higher risk.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:24.770
We have to change our whole culture,

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:27.923
about how we treat LGBT
young people in the church.

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:39.580
- I've met a lot of Mama Dragons

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:42.000
because I went and met them for lunch,

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.380
and then I told them about the group

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.580
and asked if they wanted to be a part.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:47.090
Hey, Jill.

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:48.890
So meeting with them one on one

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:51.643
and letting them share
anything they wanna share.

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:56.810
- Anna was afraid to come out to us,

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:58.910
before she came out she was telling us,

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:00.670
oh, there's a kid at school who's gay,

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.320
and he's being bullied;

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:04.410
but it's like, that was her.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:06.695
And she was afraid to tell us that.

00:06:06.695 --> 00:06:08.004
- She wanted to see what
your response would be.

00:06:08.004 --> 00:06:08.900
- Mm-hmm.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:10.970
She was testing the waters,
you know what I mean?

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.440
It's like if, you know,
are my parents gonna say,

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.050
"Well, don't hang out with that kid,

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:18.883
"stay away from that kid,"
you know, it makes me sad.

00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:22.890
She slept on the floor of
our bedroom for a month.

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:24.690
You know, it's like I
couldn't leave her alone

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:28.660
and knowing there are people like Alison,

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:30.180
you know, who ...

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:38.028
- Kind of experienced our worst nightmare.

00:06:38.028 --> 00:06:38.861
- Yeah.

00:06:45.969 --> 00:06:46.802
- Wanna show them your smile?

00:06:46.802 --> 00:06:49.913
Stockton was my long-awaited boy.

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:54.730
He was, the happiest kid ...

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.350
(baby babbles)

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:59.135
spoiled rotten.

00:06:59.135 --> 00:07:01.450
- [Stockton] Up, shake, lay.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:04.900
- I would say Stockton
was very comfortable

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:07.900
with being gay;

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:11.003
I think Stockton was very
uncomfortable with being alone.

00:07:15.533 --> 00:07:18.580
(dramatic music)

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:22.713
- That was June 27th of 2016.

00:07:26.521 --> 00:07:27.910
If someone would've told me that,

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:30.650
I would be coming back
to my son being gone,

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:32.613
I wouldn't have ever guessed it.

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:36.900
(dramatic music)

00:07:37.801 --> 00:07:39.062
- I don't know;

00:07:39.062 --> 00:07:43.027
I don't know what kind of
just pushed him that day.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:47.080
I think that's one of the hardest things,

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.863
not knowing, you know, as a mom,

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:54.340
and if I could've,

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:55.693
I would've done anything,

00:07:58.650 --> 00:07:59.600
to keep him here.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:13.350
- We hear about the gay kids
who are taking their lives,

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:16.400
but now it really did happen,

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.270
it wasn't just someone said it,

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:21.008
I live it; it's real.

00:08:21.008 --> 00:08:23.758
(dramatic music)

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:33.633
- You can't sit and see a kid suffer;

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:38.960
or see a kid talk about
how they're worth nothing,

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:40.800
and that their only two options is either

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:44.030
to leave the church, or to commit suicide.

00:08:44.030 --> 00:08:46.580
I've dealt with those kind
of situations with kids.

00:08:48.498 --> 00:08:51.248
(dramatic music)

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:54.930
- If I didn't have Jill,

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:57.957
part of me thinks I probably
wouldn't be here right now.

00:08:57.957 --> 00:09:00.030
How are you?

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:02.530
Suicide is something that I've
struggled with for a while.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:06.370
There was a time I even
thought that my parents

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:08.480
would rather me die than to marry a man,

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:10.340
and so it's something that,

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:13.203
logically, I thought made the most sense.

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:17.900
I was having a really,
really, really hard time,

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:20.590
and so I was talking to a friend about it,

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:24.180
and he said, "Well, I
have someone I can put

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:26.630
"you in contact with, her name is Jill

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:30.100
"and she's a Mama
Dragon," and I had no idea

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:32.433
what in the world the Mama Dragons were.

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:35.360
So it's been interesting
that, in the space

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:37.980
of a couple years, Jill has now become

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:40.253
such an integral part of my life.

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:45.110
- We're just his home; he is welcome here;

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:46.653
we love Shane as a family,

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:51.400
but I think it is taking a
long time for him to really,

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:54.300
start to realize how wonderful he is.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:57.183
He's had to go through
a lot of dark times.

00:09:58.470 --> 00:10:02.140
- It's very hard to be both openly gay

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:06.010
and a very active, serious
member of the church.

00:10:06.010 --> 00:10:08.313
You know, how do I choose between,

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:11.910
literally, two parts of who I am?

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:13.759
I think that's a challenge
that lots of people

00:10:13.759 --> 00:10:15.283
had to experience.

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:23.010
- Sometimes my youngest daughter will

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:26.450
ask me: "How do you go to a
church that hates your son?"

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:29.793
And, it's a hard question to answer.

00:10:29.793 --> 00:10:32.940
- Hey.
- Hey, how are you?

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:35.120
- I think if I were to categorize it,

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:38.263
I feel like I'm in a bit of
a faith crisis a little bit.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:41.780
I pray and sometimes I feel like,

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:44.273
you know, is anybody listening to me?

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:49.230
My relationship with
Heavenly Father and Jesus,

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:51.523
is kind of a work in progress.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:54.610
- You know religion and spirituality

00:10:54.610 --> 00:10:58.420
are two different things, so
I really decipher between,

00:10:58.420 --> 00:10:59.923
the church and the gospel;

00:10:59.923 --> 00:11:02.533
and the gospel will always be part of me.

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:07.040
- The Gospel of Jesus Christ is perfect.

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:12.083
The church is imperfect, even
though the gospel is perfect.

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:15.820
I look at, you know, the
leaders of our church today,

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:18.500
and say, well, I wish they were a little

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:19.780
more loving and compassionate

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:22.490
and understanding of the
experiences of LGBT people.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:25.910
But, for me, I know that
being a member of the church

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:28.333
is where God has called me to be.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:36.470
- I got a card from a family

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:39.482
in Idaho, oh, on the back it says,

00:11:39.482 --> 00:11:42.310
"Jill, thanks for loving
and accepting my son

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:45.920
"and for being such a positive
impact for good in his life.

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:48.447
"You will never know how
much that means to us."

00:11:48.447 --> 00:11:49.933
And that's from his mom.

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:55.133
'Course that always means a lot to me.

00:11:58.405 --> 00:12:00.988
(string music)

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.240
- [Man] This life is meant to live.

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:06.430
- [Woman] Finding one
friend, finding two friends.

00:12:06.430 --> 00:12:08.350
I can make a world of a difference.

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:11.350
- [Man] That day will come
when you can be yourself.

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:13.170
- [Woman] When you have
that support system,

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:14.623
it's sheer bliss.

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:18.010
- The Mama Dragons
mission is to help people

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:21.880
to see that there's
hope that they can find

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:24.113
a community in which they feel loved.

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:27.310
I know that if they're doing it with me,

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:29.060
they're doing it with other people.

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:32.380
- I look forward to the day when

00:12:32.380 --> 00:12:34.810
Mama Dragons doesn't need to exist.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:38.910
When having a LGBT kid is just as ordinary

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:40.610
as having a kid who's left-handed.

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:43.800
I feel like there's more Stocktons within

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:47.760
the walls of the church,
and there's more parents who

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:50.563
need to know that you can love your kid.

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:54.260
I believe that there will be a day

00:12:54.260 --> 00:12:57.336
that I will be reunited with him.

00:12:57.336 --> 00:13:00.503
And if not, I'm gonna be really pissed.

